Make the SSO entry points honor the mount path (SCRIPT_NAME).

Under sub-path hosting (sure-nix mounts the app at RAILS_RELATIVE_URL_ROOT via
Rack::URLMap), the SSO button, the mobile SSO auto-submit form and OmniAuth's
failure redirect use root-absolute "/auth/..." paths. They leave the app and
404 (e.g. https://host/auth/openid_connect instead of /sure/auth/...).
Prefix them with request.script_name / env["SCRIPT_NAME"]: empty at the root,
so this is the identity without a sub-path.

diff --git a/app/views/sessions/mobile_sso_start.html.erb b/app/views/sessions/mobile_sso_start.html.erb
--- a/app/views/sessions/mobile_sso_start.html.erb
+++ b/app/views/sessions/mobile_sso_start.html.erb
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 <!DOCTYPE html>
 <html><body>
-  <form id="sso_form" action="/auth/<%= ERB::Util.html_escape(@provider) %>" method="post">
+  <form id="sso_form" action="<%= ERB::Util.html_escape(request.script_name) %>/auth/<%= ERB::Util.html_escape(@provider) %>" method="post">
     <input type="hidden" name="authenticity_token" value="<%= form_authenticity_token %>">
   </form>
   <script>document.getElementById('sso_form').submit();</script>
diff --git a/app/views/sessions/new.html.erb b/app/views/sessions/new.html.erb
--- a/app/views/sessions/new.html.erb
+++ b/app/views/sessions/new.html.erb
@@ -65,7 +65,7 @@
         wording (brand-compliant) via the custom-icon asset, so no bespoke CSS.
       %>
       <%= render DS::Button.new(
-            href: "/auth/#{provider_name}",
+            href: "#{request.script_name}/auth/#{provider_name}",
             method: :post,
             variant: :outline,
             size: :md,
diff --git a/config/initializers/omniauth.rb b/config/initializers/omniauth.rb
--- a/config/initializers/omniauth.rb
+++ b/config/initializers/omniauth.rb
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@
     "sso_failed"
   end
 
-  Rack::Response.new([ "302 Moved" ], 302, "Location" => "/auth/failure?message=#{message}&strategy=#{strategy&.name}").finish
+  Rack::Response.new([ "302 Moved" ], 302, "Location" => "#{env["SCRIPT_NAME"]}/auth/failure?message=#{message}&strategy=#{strategy&.name}").finish
 end
 
